Subject: [ZEROX 4/4] Add startup profile, activation and readiness telemetry

Files modified by the generated source patch:

- net/minecraft/server/Main.java
- net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
- io/papermc/paper/zerox/ZeroxBootstrap.java

Startup behavior:

- Runs the ZEROX bootstrap before Paper opens the Minecraft listener.
- Performs first-run activation on the allocated Minecraft port.
- Stores a fingerprint-bound derived token instead of the plaintext key.
- Creates `.zerox/zerox.properties` only when missing.
- Selects bounded worker and Netty thread counts from visible processors.
- Warns when Java is not 21 or the maximum heap is below 2 GiB.
- Reports elapsed startup time after Paper reaches its `Done` state.

Default generated profile:

```properties
worker-threads=auto
tnt.max-explosions-per-tick=4
tnt.max-processing-ms-per-tick=3
tnt.log-deferrals=true
```

The profile only sets JVM properties that the administrator has not already supplied. This allows explicit startup flags to override ZEROX defaults.

The activation HTTP server closes before Paper binds the same port. The post-activation handoff pause is 250 milliseconds.
